# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The first group is correctness, not size. A .env copied in puts the
# service role key into an image layer, which anybody who can pull the
# image can read; a host node_modules silently replaces the one npm ci
# installed for Alpine, and the native parts of sharp are not portable
# between the two.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules
.next
.git
.github

# Nothing below is read by `next build` (nothing in src/ reads a file off
# disk at all), and every megabyte here is uploaded to the Docker daemon
# on every build. supabase/ alone is most of a megabyte of SQL that is
# pasted into Supabase by hand and never by the app.
tests
docs
qrcode
supabase
scripts
*.md
!README.md
